# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is an ALLOWLIST, and that is deliberate.
#
# `oe package` -- the leak gate that builds a shareable bundle -- is an
# allowlist too, for the reason its own docstring gives: a denylist ships
# whatever nobody thought to exclude, and the thing nobody thinks to exclude
# here is `state/`. It holds the account map (a real email address), the
# session map that undoes every pseudonym in every report, a cost cache full
# of absolute paths and session titles, and a context database built from
# whatever source tree this machine works in. Forgetting it once publishes all
# of that, permanently, to a public repository.
#
# So: deny everything, then re-admit exactly what ships. Backups, half-written
# temp files, bundles, logs, reports, __pycache__ and every file some future
# command drops in this tree are excluded by construction -- no rule to
# remember, nothing to keep in sync, and a new leak class cannot appear by
# somebody forgetting a line.
#
# To admit a new file, name it here AND in oe/package.py (ROOT_FILES or
# TREES). Those two lists disagreeing is itself a finding: `oe package`
# compares them (see package.drift) and reports the difference.
#
# Ordering rule, which is why every directory appears three times: git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so each directory is
# re-admitted (`!oe/`) before its contents are narrowed (`oe/*` then
# `!oe/*.py`). This is flat on purpose -- a subdirectory of oe/ or hooks/
# would need its own trio of lines, which is the moment to ask whether it
# should ship at all.
#
# .gitignore does nothing about a file that is ALREADY tracked, so CI asserts
# the tracked list separately (.github/scripts/leak_gate.py).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*

# --- documentation and repository scaffolding ---
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!VERSION
!LICENSE
!README.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!SECURITY.md

# The README is sharded into docs/ so the landing page stays readable. Flat,
# like oe/ and hooks/: a subdirectory here would need its own trio of lines,
# which is the moment to ask whether it should ship at all.
!docs/
docs/*
!docs/*.md

# --- the tool ---
!install.py
!extract_pricing.py
!config.example.json

!oe/
oe/*
!oe/*.py

!hooks/
hooks/*
!hooks/*.py

# bin/oe, bin/oe-watch and bin/oe-repair are extensionless on purpose. They are
# named one by one rather than admitted as `bin/*`, so bin/oe.bak or bin/oe.tmp
# cannot ride along on the same rule.
#
# oe-repair is the rescue script, and it is the one file here that MUST ship: it
# is what a user runs when a hook entry points at a script that is gone and
# Claude Code cannot make a single tool call. oe/package.py admits it already
# (TREES["bin"] is None, i.e. any extensionless file), so leaving it out of this
# list would have put it in exactly the state package.drift calls out -- shipped
# in a bundle, absent from a clone -- and the rescue path would be missing on
# precisely the machines that install by `git clone`.
!bin/
bin/*
!bin/oe
!bin/oe-watch
!bin/oe-repair

# --- continuous integration ---
!.github/
.github/*
!.github/workflows/
.github/workflows/*
!.github/workflows/*.yml
!.github/scripts/
.github/scripts/*
!.github/scripts/*.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces. The `*` above already excludes every one of these; they are
# repeated here, LAST, because the last matching rule wins -- so a future
# `!*.json` or `!oe/**` cannot quietly re-admit them.
#
# config.json is machine-local twice over: it carries this machine's
# reports_root, and `oe guard mode ...` rewrites it at runtime. A tracked copy
# would publish a local path AND make the documented `git pull` update fail on
# a dirty tree. Copy config.example.json if you want to tune something; with
# no config.json at all the code defaults apply, which is the supported
# zero-config case.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
state/
reports/
config.json
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.tmp
*.orig
*.rej
*.log
*.tar.gz
*.tar.gz.part
replaced-statusline*.json
settings-baseline*.json
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
.claude/
